   133	## 2. Runtime facts that constrain the design
   134	
   135	| # | Fact | Source | Consequence |
   136	|---|---|---|---|
   137	| F1 | Budget per turn: `actTimeout = 1` s. Excess comes from a per-seat bank of `remainingOverageTime = 60` s. The agent times out when the excess exceeds the remaining bank. | json:9,128; agent.py:220; core.py:631 | Steady-state turns must be well under 1 s. Only the first turn may draw on the bank. |
   138	| F2 | A file agent is `exec`'d **lazily inside the first timed call**. `sys.path` gains the agent directory only during `exec`. | agent.py:51–59,146–149 | Imports, weight load and warm-up all bill to turn 0. A late import inside `agent()` of a **bundled** module not already in `sys.modules` can fail to resolve, because the agent directory has left `sys.path` [S3]. Standard-library and image-installed packages still import. Rule: import every bundled `owl` module at module top level. |
   139	| F3 | The loader takes the **last callable** in the module globals, and passes `(obs, config)` truncated to its arg count. | agent.py:64,150–154 | `agent` must be the last callable defined in `main.py`. Test with the real loader. |
   140	| F4 | The local loader writes `configuration["__raw_path__"] = raw` before each call. | agent.py:150 | Passing `config` straight through breaks the Rust envelope (`config.rs:76`: "unknown configuration key"). The wrapper must build the game configuration from an allowlist (§3). |
   141	| F5 | An exception becomes `ERROR` and a late action becomes `TIMEOUT`; each sets that agent's reward to `None`. A returned action goes through `process_schema` with defaults. `default_schema` replaces a non-dict value (`None`, a list, a string) with the schema's default PASS action, which then validates. Only a dict that fails the JSON schema becomes `INVALID` [R5]. | core.py:279–289,636; utils.py:150–195 | `ERROR`/`TIMEOUT`/`INVALID` lose the episode, so the process boundary needs a guarded default action (§5). A wrong-typed return is **silently** normalized to PASS, not flagged, so qualification validates the raw returned action before Kaggle normalizes it. |
   142	| F6 | The default action is `{"farmer":["PASS"],"hands":[],"market":[]}`. Invalid commands are silent no-ops in the engine. | json action; AGENTS.md:68 | This is a safe fallback action that the schema accepts. |
   143	| F7 | `episodeSteps 720`: the agent is called for 719 transitions per seat. The final DONE step is not acted on. At termination the interpreter overwrites **every** seat's status with `DONE` (kaggriculture.py:960–963), including one that was `ERROR`/`TIMEOUT`/`INVALID` in the same step [R5]. | core.py:296–299; interpreter:960–964 | The local episode's denominator is 719 turns per seat. Final statuses cannot prove a clean episode: qualification inspects every recorded step's status and counts actual agent calls. |
   144	| F8 | `runTimeout` is inherited at 1200 s. Staff say production runs both agents in parallel. The local file-agent path is **sequential** (`is_parallelizable` only for URL agents). | schemas.json:71; core.py:740; topic 739874 | Locally, both seats' turns add up against 1200 s, which bounds how slow the local episode may be. |
   145	| F9 | Observations reach the agent as `Struct` (a dict subclass) locally, which preserves insertion order. In production they arrive as JSON. The client-side JSON serialization (agent.py:91) does not by itself establish that production preserves the engine's key order [S4]. | utils.py:105; agent.py:91 | Serialize with `json.dumps` without `sort_keys`. Inventory and shed rank channels depend on insertion order. Root `serde_json` has `preserve_order` (`Cargo.toml:24`). Production ordering stays an unverified risk (§13 Q6). The local episode proves only the local path. |
   146	| F10 | The competition image is built from `gcr.io/kaggle-images/python:v163` (unpinned master). The starter's image is a May 2026 `python-simulations` digest with Python 3.11. | WebFetch; `Dockerfile.kaggle` | The current Kaggriculture runtime image, its Python minor version and its torch version are **unverified**. The abi3-py311 extension covers any CPython ≥ 3.11, but glibc and the CPU architecture still matter (§6). |
   147	| F11 | The validation episode plays the agent against a copy of itself. Only the latest 2 submissions count for the final leaderboard. | Evaluation page | A new submission displaces an older one from final evaluation. That is an owner decision (§11). |
   148	
   149	## 3. The `agent(obs, config)` wrapper
   150	
   151	New files (Claude stream):
   152	
   153	- `python/kaggriculture_main.py`: the entrypoint, copied to `main.py` in the
   154	  tarball.
   155	- `python/owl/agent/kaggriculture_agent.py`: the agent class.
   156	- `python/owl/kaggriculture/kaggle_view.py`: the observation and configuration
   157	  view.
   158	
   159	Isaiah's Orbit `Agent` stays unchanged. It is Orbit-shaped: recurrent state,
   160	LoRA/int8 modes, `min_fleet_size`. The shared pieces move into small helpers
   161	used by both, not copies: thread pinning, checkpoint-config loading,
   162	`meta`-device construction plus `load_state_dict(strict=True)`, and the timing
   163	log.
   164	
   165	`main.py` does this at module top level (F2):
   166	
   167	1. Set `OMP_NUM_THREADS`/`MKL_NUM_THREADS`, then `torch.set_num_threads(N)` and
   168	   `set_num_interop_threads(1)`. N comes from the latency receipt (§7). The
   169	   default is 1, as in Isaiah's `main.py`. A second
   170	   `set_num_interop_threads` call in one process raises (confirmed by a
   171	   read-only probe in the review), so every test or harness that loads
   172	   `main.py` does it in a fresh process [R4].
   173	2. Import `owl` and call `owl.rs.assert_release_build()`.
   174	3. Load `models/primary/config.yaml` and `checkpoint.pt`, and build the model on
   175	   CPU in fp32.
   176	   - Override **only** the runtime dispatch flag `force_flash_attn` to false. It
   177	     is not a weight, and CUDA FlashAttention cannot run on CPU.
   178	   - Reject any checkpoint or config carrying hidden-state or recurrent keys, per
   179	     the [stateless constraints](../../../cookbook/decisions/the-policy-is-stateless-and-observation-only.md).
   180	   - Call `model.eval()`.
   181	   - Run one warm-up forward on a bundled fixture observation, so turn 0 pays
   182	     the warm-up once and inside the 60 s bank.
   183	4. Define `agent(obs, config)` last (F3).
   184	
   185	`agent(obs, config)` runs under `torch.inference_mode()`:
   186	
   187	1. **View.** Build `view = {"step","day","hour","farms","market","town"}` from
   188	   `obs`, the own `private`, `seat = obs["player"]`, and a game configuration.
   189	   - The configuration keeps the keys of the pinned `kaggriculture.json`
   190	     `configuration` block plus the framework keys `actTimeout`, `runTimeout`
   191	     and `seed`. It drops `__raw_path__` (F4) and any other key, logging each
   192	     dropped name once.
   193	   - Use explicit key reads (no `getattr`) and `json.dumps` without
   194	     `sort_keys` (F9).
   195	   - `remainingOverageTime`, `player` and any seed never reach the model. Seat
   196	     only selects which row is written.
   197	2. **Encode** with the Rust seat binding (§4) into a preallocated `[1,1,…]`
   198	   `KaggricultureObsBatch` of CPU tensors (allocated once and reused).
   199	   - `check_contract()` requires `[E, 2]` and stays strict for every
   200	     environment and training path. The inference path uses a separate,
   201	     explicitly scoped single-seat validator
   202	     (`check_single_seat_contract()`): the same per-field dtype, trailing
   203	     shape, range and finiteness checks with a leading shape of exactly
   204	     `[1, 1]` [R6].
   205	   - Tests: the two-seat validator rejects `[1,1]`; the single-seat validator
   206	     rejects `[1,2]`, `[2,1]` and `[2,2]`; both reject the same corrupted field;
   207	     the model's forward accepts a `[1,1]` batch.
   208	3. **Forward.** Call `model(obs_batch, deterministic=True)`. Greedy decoding is
   209	   Isaiah's packaged default (`agent_config.yaml: deterministic: true`). A
   210	   sampled mode is an explicit config switch, never a silent default.
   211	4. **Decode.** Call native `kaggriculture_decode(tokens[0,0], length, actors,
   212	   order_limit, hire_limit)` from Task 1.4. `hire_limit` is read from the
   213	   checkpoint's `action_spec` (`KaggricultureActionConfig.hire_limit`), never
   214	   hardcoded [S1]; a missing or non-Kaggriculture `action_spec` is a load-time
   215	   error. The actor count comes from the own `actor_mask[..., :241]` and the
   216	   order limit from `order_limits`, as `briefs/1.5.md:231` requires. Return
   217	   the parsed dict: `farmer`, `hands`, `market`, in canonical form.
   218	   - The wrapper validates that dict before returning it: a `dict` with exactly
   219	     those three keys, each a list of strings, parsable by the native grammar
   220	     [R5]. In strict mode (§5) a failure raises; otherwise the guard returns F6
   221	     and counts the failure.
   222	5. **Log.** Print one compact line per turn: step, encode/forward/decode ms,
   223	   remaining overage, action length. Kaggle keeps 10k characters per step.
   224	
   225	No state carries between turns except the loaded weights and the reusable
   226	buffers. The buffers are fully overwritten each turn; a test asserts that
   227	poisoning them before a call leaves the output unchanged.
   228	
   229	## 4. Encoder: same Rust code as training, not a Python fallback
   230	
   231	The existing binding needs both seats' private state (full `TraceHeader`). A
   232	live agent sees only its own. The native env and BC preparation have both.
   233	
   234	Add `encode_kaggriculture_seat_into(view_json: str, seat: int, *, <the 29
   235	named buffers with leading shape [1,1]>)`. It must be:
   236	
   237	- in `src/kaggriculture/mod.rs`, validated through the same `ObservationConfig`
   238	  and public-context checks;
   239	- written through **the same `write_seat`** that `write_env` calls;
   240	- given a shape-valid empty rival private (an empty map per rival actor, empty
   241	  shed and seeds). Contract principle 1 says the rival's private state never
   242	  reaches the own row, and a test proves it (T1).
   243	
   244	A Python encoder that reproduces the tensors is **rejected as the plan**. It
   245	would be a second implementation of every contract channel, including float32
   246	scaling and rank semantics. The rebuild removed exactly that duplication
   247	(plan C4/C6). It is reopened only if §6 proves the extension cannot load on
   248	Kaggle. Even then it must pass the same byte-identity corpus as T1, and the
   249	owner is told.
   250	
   251	## 5. Error boundary (a deliberate exception to fail-fast)
   252	
   253	An exception inside `agent()` loses the game (F5). So `agent()` catches
   254	`Exception`, prints the traceback with its step, increments a module counter,
   255	and returns the default action F6. This matches Isaiah's `b7185e5`.
   256	
   257	Qualification must never hide an error behind this guard. Every test,
   258	benchmark and the local episode run with `KAGGRICULTURE_AGENT_STRICT=1`, which
   259	re-raises, including on a returned action that fails the wrapper's validator
   260	(§3 step 4). A qualifying run must also report `caught_errors == 0`. Because
   261	Kaggle silently normalizes a non-dict return to PASS (F5), the harness also
   262	records every raw value `agent()` returns, before `process_schema`, and
   263	requires each to pass the same validator [R5]. Kaggle does
   264	not set the variable. Import-time failures (missing `.so`, bad checkpoint) are
   265	not caught, because the validation episode should fail loudly.
   266	
   267	## 6. Building the native extension for Kaggle
   268	
   269	- **Primary route (the starter's).** `Dockerfile.kaggle` builds `owl.rs` inside
   270	  Kaggle's own `linux/amd64` image, so glibc and CPython match by construction.
   271	  The `abi3-py311` module (`rs.abi3.so`) loads on any CPython ≥ 3.11. Rename the
   272	  image tag from `orbit-wars:kaggle` to a game-neutral tag. Make the
   273	  entrypoint selectable (`--entrypoint python/kaggriculture_main.py`); the
   274	  script currently hardcodes `python/main.py`.
   275	- **Repair the dependency-fetch layer [R1].** Before `cargo fetch --locked`,
   276	  `Dockerfile.kaggle` must also copy the `engine_rs` path dependency: at least
   277	  `engine_rs/Cargo.toml` plus whatever sources its manifest needs to resolve
   278	  (`COPY engine_rs/ engine_rs/` is the simple form; it gives up some layer
   279	  caching, which is acceptable). The vendored engine bytes are copied, never
